        "event": "Dense Fog Advisory",
        "headline": "Dense Fog Advisory issued June 11 at 2:35AM AKDT until June 11 at 9:00AM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Visibility as low as one quarter mile in dense fog.\n\n* WHERE...NW Kenai Peninsula and SW Kenai Peninsula, from Soldotna\nand Nikiski south to Anchor Point.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 AM AKDT this morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Hazardous driving conditions due to low visibility.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A band of locally dense fog has developed\nalong the western Kenai Peninsula coast. This band of fog has\nmoved over the Sterling Highway from Soldotna and Kenai south to\nAnchor Point. The fog will likely pers",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Anchorage AK",
        "effective": "2026-06-11T02:35:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-06-11T09:00:00-08:00",
        "areas": "SW Kenai Peninsula; NW Kenai Peninsula",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Execute",
        "instruction": "A dense fog advisory means visibilities will frequently be reduced\nto less than one quarter mile. If driving, slow down, use your\nheadlights, and leave plenty of distance ahead of you.",
        "lat": null,
        "lng": null
      },
